      "urpx:forRatePlan": {
        "@id": "gpc:fpa"
      },
      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "gpc:cc-fpa-2026-06-01",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "gpc:cc-fpa-2026-06-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 7 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Voltage level and franchise fee location. FCR-27's three voltage levels and MFF-11's two locations are crossed in one ProfileAlternatives set of six alternatives, because URPX v0.5.1 allows one set per PlanElements and the franchise fee's energy subtotal must include that voltage level's fuel prices. A consumer selects one alternative, for example Secondary Distribution inside city limits. (2) Municipal Franchise Fee base. MFF-11 applies to the total revenues of each bill, which include the ECCR-15 and DSM-C-15 amounts. Its multiplier Prices here are based on the energy-and-fuel subtotal and on the non-energy charges' Prices, not on the ECCR and DSM-C multiplier Prices, so the franchise fee on those two amounts, about 0.29 percent of the base bill inside city limits at FPA's 65 percent rider base, is not carried. (3) Excess Reactive Demand. Where a power factor below 95 percent lagging is indicated, the Company may install metering for reactive demand and bills kVAR above one-third of the measured kW at $0.43 per kVAR. The JSON-LD carries the $0.43 on a calculated MetricInput whose formula is text in its CalculationMethod; a consumer has to compute the excess kVAR, and supplies none for a customer the Company does not meter for it. (4) Customer-specific Off-Peak rate. The Off-Peak rate is (Off-Peak Charges - Basic Service Charge x 12) / Off-Peak kWh, where Off-Peak Charges are Total Charges less the On-Peak kWh at the On-Peak rate, and Total Charges are the firm tariff and riders applied to the customer's Customer Baseline Load plus forecasted RTP prices on its expected incremental consumption, less the forecasted hourly average marginal fuel cost. The JSON-LD defines Off-Peak energy as a PriceDefinition with no Price, so a modeled bill carries no Off-Peak energy charge, and the ECCR, DSM and franchise fee on it are missing too. (5) Offer and eligibility conditions. FPA is offered periodically, as the Company determines, to customers on FPA-3 Part 1 since 2010 or on Real Time Pricing for three consecutive years, and the Demand Plus Energy Credit tariff does not apply to them. They are stated in the eligibility rule's description. (6) Minimum Monthly Bill. The sheet sets it at the $245.03 Basic Service Charge plus ECCR, the applicable DSM schedule and the Municipal Franchise Fee, and no Price carries it. Every price here is positive, so a bill on these prices alone is never below it. (7) Term of Contract. The greater of the time remaining on the customer's RTP service contract or one year, renewed automatically each year unless terminated with 30 days' written notice before the anniversary. Nothing is priced by it and it is not carried.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-19T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
